# Publish only when everything is green

Before creating or pushing a stable release tag (`vX.Y.Z` without `-beta` / `-test`):

1. Local `pre-publish-check` must end in **READY**.
2. Push the release commit to `main` first.
3. Wait until **all** GitHub checks for that commit are `success`:
   - Android Build & Sign
   - CodeQL Advanced (every matrix job)
   - Any other required check on the commit
4. Only then push the tag so the in-app updater can see `releases/latest`.
5. If any check is red, in progress, or cancelled: **do not tag**. Fix and re-run until green.

Compiling locally is not enough. Verify Actions status in this session before publishing.
